72 720 Td
(Banks using IMA calculate market risk capital requirements based on value-at-risk \(VaR\)) Tj
T*
(and expected shortfall \(ES\) models.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Operational Risk RWA) Tj
T*
(4.1 Basic Indicator Approach \(BIA\)) Tj
T*
(Operational risk capital = 15% of average annual gross income over previous three years.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 Standardized Approach \(TSA\)) Tj
T*
(Operational risk capital calculated by applying regulatory factors to business line) Tj
T*
(gross income.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.3 Advanced Measurement Approach \(AMA\)) Tj
T*
(Banks using AMA develop internal models to estimate operational risk capital.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Securitization Exposures) Tj
T*
(5.1 Securitization Framework) Tj
T*
(The securitization framework includes the standardized approach, external ratings-based) Tj
T*
(approach, and internal assessment approach.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.2 Risk Weights) Tj
T*
(Risk weights for securitization exposures range from 20% to 1,250% based on external) Tj
T*
(ratings or internal assessments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Counterparty Credit Risk) Tj
T*
(6.1 Current Exposure Method \(CEM\)) Tj
T*
(The CEM calculates counterparty credit risk exposures for derivatives and securities) Tj
T*
(financing transactions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6.2 Standardized Approach for Counterparty Credit Risk \(SA-CCR\)) Tj
T*
(SA-CCR provides a more risk-sensitive method for calculating counterparty credit risk) Tj
T*
(exposures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6.3 Internal Model Method \(IMM\)) Tj
T*
(Banks using IMM calculate counterparty credit risk exposures using internal models.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Credit Risk Mitigation) Tj
T*
(7.1 Eligible Collateral) Tj
T*
(- Cash) Tj
T*
(- Gold) Tj
T*
(- Debt securities) Tj
T*
(- Equities) Tj
T*
(- UCITS units) Tj
T*
(- Mutual fund units) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7.2 Financial Guarantees) Tj
T*
(Credit protection provided by eligible guarantors can reduce risk weights.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. RWA Reporting Requirements) Tj
ET
endstream
